story.append(PageBreak());p('The math and its boundary','title');p('The problem is finite-horizon stochastic control, with causal actions and a joint funding constraint. An exact solution is conditional on the specified model; simulation cannot establish what is universally best.')
p('State and admissible actions','h');p('State includes liquid units, settled cash, pending sale receipts, fixed property units, arrears, remaining known calls and observed market history. A fully risk-constrained dynamic program also needs running path-loss/payment-event statistics. Sales cannot exceed holdings. Purchases plus fees cannot exceed settled cash. Sales enter the settlement queue; due calls debit cash; arrears persist.')
p('Objective: maximize -T log E[exp(-X_H/T)], with T=$10M and X_H = cash + marked remaining units/property + pending receipts - arrears. Paid withdrawals are already deducted. Controls cannot observe future returns or random future liabilities. The implementation rejects scenario-varying future liability amounts.','small')
p('Constraints and actual search','h');p('Long-only, no leverage, fixed unsold property; joint paid-all target 99%; dated arrears and shadow path/terminal CVaR-type screens under reference and entropy-pooled nominal/stressed measures. The same executed-policy judge is applied to every baseline. An old additive W1 reserve is a heuristic stress screen here, NOT a valid nonlinear-feedback DRO certificate. No confidence-calibrated uncertainty ball is claimed.')
p('Four risky logits relative to cash, plus shared coefficients for funding ratio, remaining fixed liabilities, observed drawdown and trailing four-week momentum. Eight bounded parameters; differential evolution, 40-vector population, eight generations, 360 evaluations, no polishing. Training penalty is a search device, not an exact constrained solver. Validation screens the top 12 training-feasible candidates. Primary train100 / validation4x200 / final4x400 paths per law.','small')
p('What was actually checked','h');p('Accounting conservation with fees and pending receipts; no future-price leakage; delayed cash cannot pay early; same first action for attribution; pro-rata withdrawal arithmetic; strict judge rejects unpaid calls; random future liabilities/rent rejected; actual multi-year annual turnover; fixed snapshot truth; pathwise relaxation dominance. A tiny two-period action-grid Bellman calculation equals exhaustive nonanticipative enumeration. That equality proves only that tiny finite problem, not the full policy optimum.')
p('Remaining work before economic conclusions','h');p('A tighter certified bound or exact solvable formulation; realistic calibrated costs, taxes and settlement; a justified long-run return/expense law; chronological out-of-sample evaluation. Property index returns and assumed dependence are not executable property liquidity. No client preference parameter was estimated. No default, holding or account was changed.','small')
